{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792352802,"nonce":"eJz0fuo+uXM7yWd82Lfto2tjvEw=","title":"DropdownMenuItem and ContextMenuItem take no icon","message":"**What is missing**\n\n`DropdownMenuItemProps` is `{onSelect, shortcut, destructive, disabled, id}`, and the item is built as a label and a shortcut. A menu whose items are contributed by an extension needs an icon on an item. RayDE puts a flex `div` with the text and an `icon` inside the item's children (the `.ui-menu-item-label` part, which `InlineFlow.attach` wraps). That works with the icon at the label's right end, but the icon cannot sit after the shortcut or in a column, and a leading icon made labels wrap (\"Reveal in Finder\" onto two lines) and the menu the wrong width, because the flow's intrinsic width does not count a block flex child's content.\n\n**Asked for**\n\nAn optional `icon:SvgDocument` on `DropdownMenuItem`, which `ContextMenuItem` inherits, with its placement decided in the component: either a leading column that is reserved when any sibling has an icon, or a trailing slot after the shortcut. RayDE's design wants it at the right.\n\n**Open**\n\nWhich placement. A leading column is the usual one; a trailing slot is what RayDE wants. It could be a prop of the menu (`iconSide`). Not scheduled. Reported by RayDE's session (its issue 4a42535 covers the second request below).","files":null}]}